      "id": "whileSavings",
      "label": "While Loop — Savings Target",
      "code": [
        "var balance = 4",
        "var week = 0",
        "let target = 25",
        "",
        "while balance < target {",
        "    week += 1",
        "    let deposit = week * 3",
        "    balance += deposit",
        "",
        "    if balance > target {",
        "        balance = target",
        "    }",
        "}"
      ],
      "practice": {
        "title": "Changing Variables Challenge",
        "prompt": "Trace balance, month and deposit. On which month does the loop stop, and what is the final balance?",
        "code": "var balance = 5\nvar month = 0\nlet target = 30\n\nwhile balance < target {\n    month += 1\n    let deposit = month * 4\n    balance += deposit\n\n    if balance > target {\n        balance = target\n    }\n}",
        "explanation": "Deposits increase each month: 4, 8, 12 and 16. The balance moves 5 → 9 → 17 → 29 → 45, then the conditional caps it at 30.",
        "answer": "Month 1: deposit = 4, balance = 9\nMonth 2: deposit = 8, balance = 17\nMonth 3: deposit = 12, balance = 29\nMonth 4: deposit = 16, balance = 45\n\n45 > 30, so balance becomes 30.\n\nLoop stops after month 4.\nFinal balance = 30"
      },
      "steps": [
        {
